      "explanation": "The per-drug Pearson of 1.6.1 averages `evaluation.pearson` over the drugs of a split. That function returns 0.0 for a constant prediction, and a drug with one pair has a constant prediction, so such drugs count as 0.0. v2 computes it with `_grouped_evaluation`, the shared rule of the per-drug comparison plots: a drug whose predictions or response are constant, or with fewer than two pairs, is undefined and skipped, so a baseline that predicts a constant per drug has no per-drug Pearson (the panel leaves it out) where 1.6.1 draws 0.000.",
