  "findings": [
    "1.6.1 keeps the NaiveMeanEffectsPredictor as a baseline row of the leaderboard and of the critical difference diagram (normalized against itself: PCC 0, RMSE and raw metrics of its own predictions). `ExperimentResult.normalize` of v2 used to drop it; it now returns array-free summaries of the reference runs in `reference_runs`, which the leaderboard table and the critical difference data frame list.",
    "1.6.1 reports the RMSE and the raw Pearson of the unnormalized predictions next to the normalized Pearson. v2 `normalize` replaces the run by its residuals, so the unnormalized pooled metrics and the per-drug Pearson are kept on the run (`RunResult.raw_metrics`, `raw_per_drug_pearson`).",
    "The per-drug Pearson of 1.6.1 averages `evaluation.pearson` over the drugs of a split. That function returns 0.0 for a constant prediction, and a drug with one pair has a constant prediction, so such drugs count as 0.0. v2 computes it with `_grouped_evaluation`, the shared rule of the per-drug comparison plots: a drug whose predictions or response are constant, or with fewer than two pairs, is undefined and skipped, so a baseline that predicts a constant per drug has no per-drug Pearson (the panel leaves it out) where 1.6.1 draws 0.000."
  ],
